# Make `engines` in package.json a GUARD rather than a suggestion.
#
# npm only enforces `engines` when engine-strict is set; without this file it prints an EBADENGINE warning
# and installs anyway. Nuxt 4 requires ^22.19.0 || ^24.11.0 || >=26.0.0, so a developer on Node 20 or 22.14
# installed successfully and then hit an opaque Nuxt failure that never named the Node version.
#
# CI was already covered — but by `.nvmrc` via actions/setup-node, NOT by `engines`. This closes the
# developer-machine half, which is the half the "pinned NOWHERE" note in Story 23.5 was actually about.
# [Story 23.5 code review 2026-08-08]
engine-strict=true
